The trigger of an omission may be the stimulus itself, the request the stimulus approach delivers to the target. The stimulus is not a supplied observation and not an evidence ref, so selected_evidence cites no entry for it; state that trigger in stimulus_approach and in the observation_claim branches. The plan check still requires a stated trigger: it passes when the condition's own comparisons scope the omission to another operation, and otherwise when selected_evidence cites a supplied observation of another operation's result (or binds it from supplied input, or lists it in prerequisite evidence) or selects that operation. When the inventory supplies no observation of another operation and the condition scopes the omission to none, the package is refused: the run cannot evidence when the call was due.
